\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Weaker At BRL2.932 To Dollar Thu  \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 20:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened slightly Thursday as sovereign bond prices fell overseas, driving up interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The weakness occurred even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't buy dollars under its new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy designed to rebuild scant foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL2.932 to the dollar, compared with BRL2.919 at Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 The real has been in a weakening cycle for more than a week, as fears about interest-rate hikes abroad and inflation at home pressure Brazilian assets.  \par \par \uc2 Also, the real is also being pinched by periodic dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under its new policy aimed at rebuilding reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is frequently buying dollars to help reduce potential volatility and weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help make it more competitive for exporters to sell their goods.  \par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy is aimed at helping \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  close its external financing gap in 2004 after the nation last year recorded its first current account surplus in about a decade.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to not roll over $1.13 billion in dollar-linked debt and, instead, pay it off. Since mid-2003, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced the amount of dollar-linked paper in the market to help reduce potential volatility and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness if there were any economic shocks in the future.  \par \par \uc2 -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040205e025000tv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
