\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Weaker In Early Trade At BRL2.940 Per Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2004\par 15:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened in early trade Thursday as traders braced for potential dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sovereign bonds overseas fell.  \par \par \uc2 At 1400 GMT, the real was at BRL2.940 to the dollar, compared with BRL2.919 at Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 The real has been in a weakening cycle for more than a week, as fears about interest rate hikes abroad and inflation at home pressure Brazilian assets. Also, the real is being pressured by periodic dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under its new policy aimed at rebuilding reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is buying dollars to help reduce potential volatility and weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help make it more competitive for exporters to sell their goods.  \par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy is aimed at helping \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  close its external financing gap in 2004 after the nation last year recorded its first current account surplus in about a decade.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opted to not roll over $1.13 billion in dollar-linked debt and instead pay if off. Since mid-2003, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced the amount of dollar-linked paper in the market to help reduce potential volatility and weakness if there were any shocks to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2