\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Weaker; Ctrl Bk Starts Buying Dlrs Again  \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2004\par 20:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real finished Wednesday on a slightly weaker note after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  returned to the market and started buying dollars again.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.919 to the dollar after it strengthened Tuesday to BRL2.918 to the dollar from BRL2.944.  \par \par \uc2 The real, which lifted to as much as BRL2.900 to the dollar, could have ended the session in a stronger position had the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not bought an unspecified amount of dollars at the rate of BRL2.908.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is buying dollars to help build its international reserves, reduce potential volatility, and weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help make it more competitive for exporters to sell their wares.  \par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy is aimed at helping \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  close its external financing gap in 2004 after the nation last year recorded its first current account surplus in about a decade.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has denied it has set a floor and a ceiling for the real but it looks like it isn't prepared to let the real strengthen beyond the BRL2.900 to the dollar level," said a Sao Paulo-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 Meantime, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it wouldn't roll over $1.13 billion in dollar-linked debt and that it would buy the debt back. Since mid-2003, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced the amount of dollar-linked paper in the market to help reduce potential volatility and weakness if there were any shocks to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate in the future.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1478; anthony.dovkants@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040204e024000r9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
