\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Strengthens Nearly 1% To BRL2.918 Per Dlr   \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2004\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real strengthened nearly 1% Tuesday against the dollar as investors shook off a week of plunging markets and many of the country's stocks and bonds rallied.   \par \par \uc2 The real finished Tuesday at BRL2.918 for each dollar, compared with Monday's close of BRL2.944. Brazil's benchmark Ibovespa stock index rose 2.3% to 22,280 as the price of Brazil's global bond maturing in 2040 rose one point to 108 3/4.   \par \par \uc2 A recovery of the prices of developing nations bonds also helped to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Sovereign spreads indexed on J.P. Morgan's Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus (EMBI+) tightened as the gap between the yield of the EMBI+ and comparable U.S. Treasurys narrowed six basis points to 438 basis points over Treasurys.   \par \par \uc2 What's more, for the third day in a row, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars as part of a policy to replenish international reserves. This also helped to support the real.   \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's rally suggests that investors have recovered from their disappointment with news Monday that Standard & Poor's was unlikely to upgrade Brazil's credit rating this year.   \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Vogel, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1480; tom.vogel@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040203e023000wi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
