\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real eases on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks edge up.   \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2004\par 15:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased slightly and stocks crept higher on Friday as investors, still smarting from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to hold interest rates this week, tiptoed back into the market after a brief sell-off.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real backtracked 0.21 percent to 2.845 per dollar in early trading, giving up the previous day's gains after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought greenbacks on the spot market for the twelfth session in a row.   \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa index , meanwhile, edge up 0.34 percent to 23,047.5 points, bouncing back slightly after an early slide into negative territory.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the market was still digesting the bank's surprise decision late Wednesday to hold its overnight lending rate at 16.5 percent, putting an end to a seven-month run of rate cuts that had propelled the Bovespa into record territory.   \par \par \uc2 "The market was already looking to take some profits before the bank's decision, and that just fed that tendency even more," said Alvaro Bandeira, a director at Agora Senior CTVM investment firm in Rio de Janeiro.   \par \par \uc2 "In the long term, the outlook is still positive, but the short term is much more problematic thanks to the rates decision. We may see some more losses, but the market is showing some resiliency."   \par \par \uc2 Telephone company Brasil Telecom Participacoes (BRTO4.SA) weighed on the Bovespa early on. Brasil Telecom's share price fell 2 percent to 16.71 reais following a report of renewed tension in the company's boardroom.   \par \par \uc2 Brazilian financial daily Valor Economico said private equity fund CVC Opportunity, which has a controlling stake in Brasil Telecom, has told Telecom Italia (TLIT.MI) it cannot regain a voting stake in the Rio-based phone company.   \par \par \uc2 The move flies in the face of a ruling last week by Brazilian regulators, who gave Telecom Italia the green light to return to Brasil Telecom.   \par \par \uc2 But while Brasil Telecom's stock waded in the red, shares in rival phone company Tele Norte Leste Participacoes (Telemar) (TNLP4.SA) chugged higher. Telemar shares, which account for 14 percent of the Bovespa index, climbed 1.97 percent to 49.80 reais.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040123e01n004i4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
