\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Ends Weaker;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again  \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2004\par 20:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakened Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and bought more dollars as part of a two-pronged policy of keeping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  competitive for exporters and rebuilding its international reserves in the long term.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.845 to the dollar after it finished at BRL2.838 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to avoid an appreciation of the real, rebuild its reserves and help Brazil close its external financing gap," said Eduardo de Faria Carvalho, chief economist at Banco Safra.  \par \par \uc2 Carvalho said Brazil is going through a positive phase and that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real would appreciate to between BRL2.40 and BRL2.60 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 That wouldn't be good if a negative external shock hit Brazil. Such an event would prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depreciate quickly and would create much volatility, he added.  \par \par \uc2 According to talk among traders, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $1 billion on the market since it announced earlier this month it would purchase dollars to rebuild its low reserves.  \par \par \uc2 As a part of this, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late Tuesday it would redeem $2.52 billion worth of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt coming due Feb. 2.  \par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came just ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision on whether to cut the reference lending rate.  \par \par \uc2 The market expects a reduction of 50 basis points to 16.00%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced the Selic rate by 10 percentage points since June to help revive Brazil's economy, which briefly plunged into recession last year.  \par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1478; anthony.dovkants@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040121e01l000pq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
