\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real falls on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks rise.   \b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2004\par 21:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the eighth session in a row, while stocks rose in heavy options-related trading as investors bet on an interest-rate cut later in the week.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real backtracked 0.39 percent to 2.84 to the dollar, with the bulk of the losses coming after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought an unspecified amount of greenbacks at 2.838 reais to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "At first it looked like the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was going to try to drive the exchange rate up higher because it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a high," said Laercio Longo, a fund manager at Unibanco Asset Management in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 "But it ended up only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  once and the market calmed down later in the day."   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a key player in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market of late, helping to beat the real back from an 18-month high early last week by aggressively snapping up dollars.   \par \par \uc2 The bank changed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy earlier this month, saying it would call dollar auctions on a regular basis to bolster its foreign reserves. Previously, state-owned Banco do Brasil (BBAS3.SA) would buy dollars on the spot market on the Treasury's behalf.   \par \par \uc2 In the stock market, the Sao Paulo exchange's benchmark Bovespa index rose 1 percent to 23,385.1 points in busy trading as investors shuffled their portfolios before options expired at midsession.   \par \par \uc2 Volume was surprisingly robust, even though many foreign investors stayed home for the day for the U.S. Martin Luther King Jr. holiday.   \par \par \uc2 Most market watchers expect stocks to trade range-bound until the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee, or Copom, emerges from its monthly interest rate meeting on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 In a Reuters poll of 20 economists last week, 15 said the bank would cut its benchmark Selic rate by a half percentage point to 16 percent. Of the remainder, four bet on a 0.75 percentage point reduction and one forecast a full point cut.   \par \par \uc2 At the Bovespa, telephone company Tele Norte Leste Participacoes (Telemar) (TNLP4.SA), the market bellwether and a favorite among options traders, helped buoy the index. Telemar shares rose 1.86 percent to 48.13 reais.   \par \par \uc2 In the energy sector, shares in Tractebel Energia (TBLE3.SA) jumped 3.41 percent to 13.96 reais after Fitch Atlantic Ratings upgraded Brazil's energy sector to stable from negative, citing improved profit margins and a positive growth outlook for 2004.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040119e01j003jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
