\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real falls on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks edge up.   \b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2004\par 15:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the eighth session running, while stocks hovered near break-even ahead of the expiration of options.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real slumped 0.57 percent to 2.845 to the dollar, with the bulk of the losses coming after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought an unspecified amount of greenbacks at 2.838 reais to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  loves to say that it isn't out to influence the exchange rate, but when it buys dollars like this it is clearly having an impact," said Sergio Machado, a fund manager at Santa Fe Portfolios in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a key player in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market of late, helping to beat the real back from an 18-month high early last week by aggressively snapping up dollars.   \par \par \uc2 The bank changed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy earlier this month, saying it would call dollar auctions on a regular basis to bolster its foreign reserves. Previously, state-owned Banco do Brasil (BBAS3.SA) would buy dollars on the spot market on the Treasury's behalf.   \par \par \uc2 In the stock market, shares seesawed in and out of the red as investors shuffled their portfolios before options expired at the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange.   \par \par \uc2 The exchange's benchmark Bovespa index was up 0.15 percent at 23,188.1 points in early afternoon trade, bouncing back slightly from an early drop into negative territory.   \par \par \uc2 Volume was modest, though, as many U.S. investors stayed home for the day for the U.S. Martin Luther King Jr. holiday.   \par \par \uc2 Most market watchers expect stocks to trade range-bound until the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee, or Copom, emerges from its monthly interest rate meeting on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 In a Reuters poll of 20 economists last week, 15 said the bank would cut its benchmark Selic rate by a half percentage point to 16 percent. Of the remainder, four bet on a 0.75 percentage point reduction and one forecast a full point cut.   \par \par \uc2 "With options expiring today and the Copom kicking off its meeting tomorrow, I don't think we'll see the market go very far either way until we know what happens with interest rates," said Carlos Camacho, a portfolio manager at GAP Asset Management in Rio de Janeiro.   \par \par \uc2 At the Bovespa, telephone company Tele Norte Leste Participacoes (Telemar) (TNLP4.SA), the market bellwether and a favorite among options traders, slipped 0.21 percent to 47.15 reais.   \par \par \uc2 On the upside, stock in long-distance phone company Embratel Participacoes (EBTP4.SA) rose 3.28 percent to 9.45 reais, while steelmaker Companhia Siderurgica Nacional (CSNA3.SA) climbed 2.69 percent to 167.54 reais.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040119e01j002dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
