\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real firm despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks down.   \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2004\par 15:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed early on Thursday even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prepared to buy dollars for the sixth session running, but the nation's stock market slumped on profit-taking.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real advanced 0.21 percent to 2.812 per dollar, buoyed by the flow of fresh greenbacks into the market stemming from a slew of recent corporate bond issues abroad, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have stabilized above the 2.80 mark after the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which showed it was aggressive and capable of influencing the exchange rate," said Jorge Kattar, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Rabobank in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a key player in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market of late, helping to beat the real back from an 18-month high in the past two sessions by snapping up dollars aggressively.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy earlier this month, saying it would call auction auctions on a regular basis to bolster its foreign reserves. Previously, state-owned Banco do Brasil would act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on the Treasury's behalf.   \par \par \uc2 Stocks, meanwhile, drifted lower for the third day in a row as investors continued to cash in on a heady rally that lifted the market to successive record highs in an early January rally.   \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa index dropped 1.25 percent to 23,106.9 points in early afternoon trade, but was still up almost 4 percent since the start of the year.   \par \par \uc2 "It's nothing to be alarmed about, it's just some profit-taking," said Alvaro Bandeira, a director at Agora Senior CTVM investment firm in Rio de Janeiro. "The market is still optimistic, so I think it will bounce back soon."   \par \par \uc2 Most shares were trading in negative territory, though a few energy stocks like Sao Paulo city power company Eletropaulo Metropolitana (ELPL4.SA) and Rio-based Light Servicos de Electricidade (LIGH3.SA) hovered on the upside.   \par \par \uc2 Eletropaulo shares rose 2.27 percent to 68.01 reais while Light stock was up 1.41 percent at 79.10 reais.   \par \par \uc2 But blue chips like long-distance telephone company Embratel Participacoes (EBTP4.SA) and state-run oil giant Petrobras (PETR4.SA) weighed on the Bovespa index.   \par \par \uc2 Embratel shares slipped 2.39 percent to 9.00 reais and Petrobras stock dropped 1.38 percent to 83.01 reais.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040115e01f0030w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
