\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real falls as cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , stocks up.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Todd Benson   \par \uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2004\par 15:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 13 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real backtracked on Tuesday after soaring to an 18-month high a day earlier, tumbling after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to put the brakes on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The real jumped a half percentage point in trading but reversed course after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in three separate auctions as part its strategy to beef up foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 By the early afternoon, the real was off 0.86 percent at 2.815 per dollar, marking a 3 percent gain since the new year began. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it purchased an unspecified amount of dollars at 2.787 and 2.798 reais to the greenback in the first two auctions, but was yet to divulge the sale price of the third.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been very effective lately when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but today it made sure it had an impact on the exchange rate," said Hideaki Iha, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Souza Barros brokerage in Sao Paulo.   \par \par \uc2 The bank also bought dollars twice on Monday, but that wasn't enough to stop the real from soaring to its highest level since late June 2002 after Brazil sold $1.5 billion in 30-year global bonds.   \par \par \uc2 Monday's rally brought the real back to where it was in late 2002 before the election of President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, a one-time fiery leftist who has since become a favorite on Wall Street by proving his mettle as a fiscal conservative.   \par \par \uc2 The bond issue, which drew demand between $6 billion and $7 billion, underscored rising investor confidence in Brazil's economic fortunes under Lula.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market has also hit successive record highs lately on hopes that the Brazilian economy, Latin America's largest, will expand between 3.5 percent and 4 percent this year after near-zero growth in 2003.   \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa index raced ahead again on Tuesday, climbing 1.12 percent to 24,507.8 points in busy trading on bets the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut interest rates next week for the eighth month in a row.   \par \par \uc2 The gains left the Bovespa up 10 percent so far since Jan. 1. Last year the Bovespa rallied a whopping 97 percent, ending a three-year losing streak.   \par \par \uc2 Shares in Companhia Vale do Rio Doce (CVRD) (VALE5.SA), the world's biggest iron ore miner, were among the early leaders. CVRD stock jumped 3.29 percent to 157 reais on news it had reached a deal to raise ore prices for its top client, steelmaker Arcelor (CELR.PA), by up to 18.6 percent.   \par \par \uc2 On the downside, shares in mobile telephone company Telesp Celular Participacoes (TSPP4.SA) fell 1.78 percent to 8.82 reais after it said it had dropped plans for now to bolster its stake in subsidiary Tele Centro Oeste (TCO) (TCOC3.SA).   \par \par \uc2 The decision came after Brazil's securities and exchange commission ruled last month that the terms of the proposed swap of 1.27 Telesp Celular shares for each outstanding TCO (TCOC4.SA) share were "contrary to existing legislation."    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040113e01d0036v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
