\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real falls on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk, stocks dip.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Todd Benson  \par \uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2003\par 21:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled more than 1 percent on Thursday, notching its biggest loss in three months amid heavy speculation that the Treasury was snapping up dollars to bolster reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The Treasury denied any responsibility for the fall.  \par \par \uc2 The real BRBY) weakened 1.25 percent to 2.94 to the greenback, its largest single-day drop since Aug. 1. That left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  20.6 percent stronger year to date.  \par \par \uc2 The losses, traders said, came after federal bank Banco do Brasil swept into the spot market and bought dollars on behalf of the Treasury, which has been actively seeking to boost the country's scant international reserves lately.  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone knew the government was going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in the market) at some point and today they didn't even try to hide it," said Hideaki Iha, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Souza Barros brokerage in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 "Banco do Brasil showed its face early on, letting everyone know that they were there."  \par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Banco do Brasil declined to comment and the Treasury denied being behind the tumble.  \par \par \uc2 "Today's movement is not related to Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Jose Antonio Gragnani, head of the Treasury's public debt department, told Reuters. "The Treasury tries to act in the most discreet way possible."  \par \par \uc2 But just last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made it easier for the Treasury to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, extending the settlement period for its dollar purchases on the spot market to six months from 90 days.  \par \par \uc2 STOCKS HIT NEW HIGH  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's stock market also fell on Thursday, slipping 0.21 percent to 18,754.5 points as investors locked in gains after hitting a new record high in early trading.  \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa index .BVSP) jumped 1.71 percent to 19,115.2 soon after the opening bell, surpassing its previous all-time high of 19,046, set on March 27, 2000.  \par \par \uc2 The early surge came on the back of news that MCI, the beleaguered U.S. phone giant formerly known as WorldCom Inc., had put its controlling stake in Brazilian long-distance carrier Embratel Participacoes up for sale.  \par \par \uc2 Embratel's ordinary shares, which have voting rights, soared 39.24 percent to 11.00 reais on the news, briefly lifting the broader market. Its preferred, or minority shares, rose 3.24 percent to 10.20 reais.  \par \par \uc2 MCI said Wednesday it had not yet identified a buyer for its 19.26 percent economic interest and 51.79 percent voting stake in Embratel, which it bought in 1998 for $2.3 billion as part of the privatization of Brazil's telecom sector.  \par \par \uc2 "The good news is that the lack of definition about whether Embratel would be sold is finally over," said Marcelo Mesquita, Brazil strategist at UBS investment bank in Rio de Janeiro.  \par \par \uc2 "Now the race is on to find out who the buyer is, and the talk is that it could be the Mexicans," he added, referring to Telefonos de Mexico, the fixed-line giant owned by telecom tycoon Carlos Slim.  \par \par \uc2 Other analysts, however, said local players like Tele Norte Leste Participacoes, or Telemar, and Brasil Telecom Participacoes were better positioned to snatch up Embratel.  \par \par \uc2 Still, both companies' shares fell on Thursday, with Telemar sliding 0.22 percent to 40.01 reais and Brasil Telecom falling 1.64 percent to 20.95 reais. (Additional reporting by Rodrigo Menderico).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031113dzbd003yx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
