\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Softer; Govt Boosts  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Pwr  \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2003\par 13:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real opened weaker Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended the settlement period for the Treasury's spot dollar purchases, boosting the government's ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at BRL2.863 to the dollar, after closing Monday at BRL2.850.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced after markets closed Monday that it would give the Treasury more time to settle dollar purchases it makes on the spot market, extending the period from three to six months. This could allow the government to buy more dollars in the short term to bolster reserves to pay down foreign debt.  \par \par \uc2 The Treasury has already bought more than $5.0 billion on the spot market this year, preventing strong dollar inflows from overseas debt issues and rising exports from making the real less competitive.  \par \par \uc2 Adding to uncertainty in the market Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to announce at the end of the session if it will refinance any of the $406 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps maturing Nov. 13. The bank isn't expected to roll over a large percentage of the swaps, which support the real by serving as a substitute for dollars for investors looking to hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk.  \par \par \uc2 Still, a steady stream of dollar inflows is expected to alleviate pressure on the real.  \par \par \uc2 The market is waiting for money to come in from debt deals recently closed by Banco Rural and Braskem, and rumors are circulating that Banco do Brasil and Unibanco are preparing to place more overseas debt, possibly worth up to $1 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say diminishing risk is paving the way for the private sector to close new debt deals abroad, keeping dollars flowing in to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 -By Hannah Karp, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1479; brazil@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031104dzb4000k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
