\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Adds To Treasury's  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Power  \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2003\par 12:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Monday extended the settlement period for the Treasury's dollar purchases on the spot market to six months from about three, a change that should substantially boost the ability of the government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Before spot market trade opened Tuesday, dollar futures were trading weaker at BRL2.895 to a dollar, compared with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's close of BRL2.850 per dollar Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The Treasury, in an attempt to reduce pressure on the country's scant net foreign reserves of about $19 billion, has been busy buying dollars on the spot market this year to meet overseas debt payments.  \par \par \uc2 The Treasury has said it bought more than $5.0 billion on the spot market this year, and plans to buy another $5.0 billion next year.  \par \par \uc2 The strategy also prevents strong dollar inflows from strengthening the real too much to the detriment of record monthly trade surpluses posted in recent months.  \par \par \uc2 Credit Suisse First Boston said in a Tuesday note that the rule change will better allow the Treasury to prepare for some $5.0 billion in debt payments due in April of next year. Between November and April, Brazil has some $7.3 billion in sovereign payments due, excluding International Monetary Fund loans.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031104dzb4000ih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
