\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Ends Unchanged At BRL2.903/Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2003\par 21:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real ended unchanged Monday in mostly quiet trading, with dollar inflows offsetting worries about a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a small rollover of dollar-linked debt later this week.  \par \par \uc2 After trading in a tight range, the real closed at BRL2.903 to the dollar, even with Friday's finish.  \par \par \uc2 Traders continued to think the government doesn't want to see the real stronger than BRL2.90 for a prolonged period of time and may indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it. Otherwise, a rising trade surplus and a narrowing current account deficit could deteriorate.  \par \par \uc2 State-run Banco do Brasil has been active buying dollars for the Treasury, in recent weeks purchasing upwards of $700 million.  \par \par \uc2 Some think more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are coming after \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week raised to 90 days from 60 days the time period in which the Treasury must settle dollar futures contracts. For other players, the 60-day rule remains in effect.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't explain its decision, but market players believe the move will make it easier for the Treasury to buy dollars in local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 In other news hitting the market, on Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will start rolling over a still unknown portion of about $2.35 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps maturing on Oct. 1.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to reduce its exposure to the securities, a tactic that in recent weeks has caused slight short-term weakening of the real.  \par \par \uc2 But helping to support the real, traders say, are inflows from corporate bond sales overseas. The market is waiting for inflows from a $500 million bond drinks giant Ambev has placed overseas.  \par \par \uc2 -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020030922dz9m000zc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
