\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Ends Weaker On Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2003\par 22:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended weaker Thursday as state-run Banco do Brasil bought dollars for the Treasury and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to snap up greenbacks below the BRL2.90 level, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Though it strengthened early to as far as BRL2.874 on expectations of a sovereign bond sale and a big debt offering by drinks giant Ambev, the real weakened during the session to end at BRL2.915 a dollar, compared with BRL2.890 per dollar at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  "The government is behaving the right way. The market thinks a real stronger than BRL2.90 would hurt exports and external accounts. This creates \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expectations," said Rodrigo Boulous, head trader at Banco Santos in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  Traders put purchases by Banco do Brasil at at least $80 million. The official explanation for these purchases is that they will allow the Treasury to honor foreign debt. But traders consider the buys \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the government has foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for its part, has no official \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  target and only operates in the market via primary dealers when liquidity problems arise. Its offers to buy dollars didn't result in purchases Thursday, traders said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't immediately available for comment. \par \par \uc2  There were some liquidity problems and few dollar buyers Thursday as good news hit the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed its third foreign bond sale this year and Ambev said it increased the size of an overseas bond to $500 million from $300 million. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday, the real was helped by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale of $482 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to roll over more than 32% of some $1.5 billion in securities expiring Sept. 17. \par \par \uc2  Inflows from rising exports and overseas debt placements have helped lift the real about 22% since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030911dz9b001ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
