\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Palocci rules out  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2003\par 02:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , April 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Antonio Palocci said on Friday the government will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the exchange rate at a more favorable rate for exporters. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar will find its own value. We cannot interfere with the exchange rate. It's inappropriate, it's an unsound macroeconomic policy ...," Palocci told reporters after visiting the Sao Paulo stock exchange. \par \par \uc2  Palocci's comment came after the real firmed against the dollar for the sixth straight session to its best close since Sept.16. It ended at 3.22 per dollar, marking a 4.4 percent gain for the week and a 10 percent advance so far in 2003. \par \par \uc2  Palocci said that Brazil's floating exchange rate policy, adopted in January 1999, was as important as inflation targets. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles also denied on Friday any plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain the exchange rate at a favorable level for exports, saying the bank would only act if there were liquidity problems. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Planning Minister Guido Mantega said that 3.20 reais per dollar would ease inflationary pressure while keeping Brazilian exports competitive. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030405dz450005r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
