\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Real Opens At BRL3.515/Dlr V BRL3.530/Dlr End Thu \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2003\par 12:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Brazil's real strengthened in early trading Friday amid capital inflows and growing investor optimism toward Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's new Workers' Party government. \par \par \uc2  By 1210 GMT (7:10 a.m. EST), the real was trading at BRL3.495 to the dollar after closing Thursday at BRL3.530. \par \par \uc2  The gains come despite news that Rio de Janeiro state defaulted on a BRL85 million debt payment - a move that raises concern about the financial health of many Brazilian states at the start of Lula's government this week. The state is asking for the government to find a solution to the problem and help it pay its workers their year-end bonus. \par \par \uc2  Usually such bad news weakens the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but a Sao Paulo-based trader said capital inflows of some $400 million were helping lift the real amid thin liquidity during the holiday season. \par \par \uc2  He added the market was also warming to a series of Workers' Party second-tier appointments to its economic team. Among those named are left-leaning economists who are members of the Workers' Party, moderate and liberal economists with solid technical and academic background, and officials who will remain in their posts after serving four years under the former President Fernando Henrique Cardoso's administration. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market continued to warm up to comments by Antonio Palocci at his inaugural speech as finance minister Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Seeking to reassure investors about a party that once advocated a debt moratorium but now says it will stick to sound economic policy, Palocci reiterated the government would work to keep inflation in check, maintain fiscal discipline to stabilize Brazil's debt to goss-domestic-product ratio. \par \par \uc2  While he didn't address the issue of full \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence directly, Palocci said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have the freedom to act in any way that it chose to ensure it met its inflationary goals. \par \par \uc2  Investors have been worried that the Workers' Party, which wants to revive \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sluggish economy, would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates prematurely and allow inflation to get out of control. \par \par \uc2  -By Anthony Dovkants; Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1478; anthony.dovkants@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030103dz13000k0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
