\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends Stronger As Mkt Warms To Lula Fin Team \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2003\par 20:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Brazil's real finished stronger Thursday as the market warmed to the latest batch of appointments to the Workers' Party's economic team and to comments that the political group will stick to sound economic discipline. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed a centavo stronger at BRL3.530 to the dollar on its first trading day of the year, and a day after Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva of the Workers' Party was sworn in as president of Brazil. \par \par \uc2  The real gained on a number of second-tier finance ministry appointments unveiled Wednesday by the Workers' Party. Among those named are left-leaning economists who are members of the Workers' Party, moderate and liberal economists with solid technical and academic background, and officials who will remain in their posts after serving four years under the former President Fernando Henrique Cardoso's administration. \par \par \uc2  "We looked for people with different backgrounds in economic thinking," Finance Minister Antonio Palocci said in a television interview Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market also warmed to comments by Palocci at his inaugural speech as finance minister Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Seeking to reassure investors about a party that once advocated a debt moratorium but now says it will stick to sound economic policy, Palocci reiterated the government would work to keep inflation in check. \par \par \uc2  Palocci stressed again that the new government would undertake the necessary fiscal discipline to stabilize Brazil's debt-to-gross-domestic-product ratio, which hit record highs last year. He added this would be the best way to reduce interest rates, which were raised three percentage points to 25% last month. \par \par \uc2  While he didn't address the issue of full \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence directly, Palocci said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have the freedom to act in any way that it chose to ensure it met its inflationary goals. \par \par \uc2  Investors have been worried that the Workers' Party, which wants to revive \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sluggish economy, would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates prematurely and allow inflation to get out of control. \par \par \uc2  He also said the government's economic goals this year would be unveiled over the coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  -By Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1478; anthony.dovkants@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030102dz12000x6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
