\par\par \b \uc2  Chile peso rises after gains for Brazilian real. \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2002\par 19:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Chile, Oct 31 (Reuters) - Chile's peso continued to firm on Thursday, following gains in the Brazilian real as traders said calm was returning to Brazilian markets following the election of leftist Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva as president. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 726.50/727.00, an appreciation of 0.99 percent compared with 733.70/734.20 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.2 percent stronger at 3.635 per dollar at midday on Thursday as investor worries that the president-elect will mishandle the country's ailing economy gave way to cautious optimism about the nation's outlook. \par \par \uc2  "I think that what is happening in Brazil is similar to what happened in Chile (in 2000) when polls gave (current center-left President) Ricardo Lagos the lead in the elections. The peso began to slide but once he was elected it recovered," said Pedro Verdugo, trader with Viajes Mercury. \par \par \uc2  Ricardo lagos, the first Chilean President to call himself a socialist since Salvador Allende was ousted in a 1973 coup, was elected by a narrow margin in 2000. \par \par \uc2  "Of course Lagos did not have the pressure of negotiating a huge public debt, as is the case in Brazil, but in any case the performance of the markets indicates that confidence is returning to the country," Verdugo added. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real lost around 40 percent of its value in 2002 before the elections, dragging the peso to historic lows of 760.50/761.00 on Oct. 10. \par \par \uc2  The peso has strengthened since on the calmer outlook in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly and indirectly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when necessary. \par \par \uc2  Traders also speculated it was looking likely that Argentina would soon reach an agreement for financial aid with the International Monetary Fund to prop up its battered economy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021031dyav0109p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
