\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends At BRL3.920/Dlr Vs BRL3.850 End Tue \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2002\par 21:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Despite a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended weaker Wednesday as concerns about the country's fiscal future and debt-servicing ability intensify ahead of Oct. 27 presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  The real finished 1.8% down at BRL3.920 to the dollar, compared with BRL3.850 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  While investors continue to fret that likely presidential victor Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will struggle to reverse the country's deteriorating financial situation, much of the pressure Wednesday came from $3.6 billion in dollar-linked debt maturing Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In a bevy of attempts, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far only refinanced about 60% of the paper. Now traders expect the debt to be paid off, increasing the country's monetary base at a time when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working to remove liquidity from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Though a rate hike Monday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 21% from 18% and tightening of reserve requirements late last week helped stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, the real has again come under pressure in what traders say is an escalating struggle for the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  And the real is expected to experience added pressure as many more dollar-linked bonds with short maturities fall due in the next several weeks. \par \par \uc2  Holders of the bonds have an incentive to bet against the real. The weaker the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bigger the return for investors that own maturing dollar-linked paper. \par \par \uc2  -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021016dyag0016y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
