\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens At 10.1470/Dlr Vs 10.0950 Wed End \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2002\par 16:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY -(Dow Jones)- Mexico's peso opened weaker against the dollar Thursday, tracking the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as that country's presidential elections approach. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City around 1435 GMT, on 48-hour spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex quoted the peso trading at a mid rate of 10.1420 per dollar against 10.0950 per dollar at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Spreads were 10.1370/10.1470 pesos per dollar, compared with MXN10.0850/10.1050 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the session, Banamex quoted the spot peso opening at a mid rate of 10.1470 per dollar on a spread of MXN10.1420/10.1520. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's first round of elections is Sunday. If front-runner Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva of the Workers' Party wins a simple majority, then the race will not go into a run off. \par \par \uc2  However, investors would rather that left-leaning Lula didn't win. Brazil is shouldering about $240 billion in government debt, a third of which is owed to foreign creditors. And investors fear that Lula may bring about a debt default in one of Latin America's two largest economies. \par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real extended losses at Thursday's open as traders hoped for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We're watching very closely what \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  does, and tomorrow should be the same," said one Mexico City-based peso trader. \par \par \uc2  He added that stock advances Thursday were helping to contain some of the peso's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average was gaining 1.6% early in the session, and Mexico's key IPC index was mirroring the rise. \par \par \uc2  -By Amy Guthrie, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5080-3453; amy.guthrie@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1027 1852 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021003dya3000ue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
