\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL \highlight\uc2  PRESS: Ctrl Bk Lifts Estimate On Real  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2002\par 17:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will spend about $1.6\par billlion more than initially projected on curbing  depreciation of the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, the Folha de Sao Paulo newspaper reported\par Sunday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its projection for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in 2002 to $9.3 billion from $7.7 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said they foresee \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at about $800 million per month through the end  of the year, compared with $500 million seen previously. \par \par \uc2  The greater-than-expected spending to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, will leave the country's next administration with fewer resources to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of  the real ($1BRL3.875). The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimates it will have about $6.8 billion on hand for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the beginning of next year, compared with a previous estimate of  $8.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 40% against the dollar this year amid investor nervousness about the outcome of the country's presidential elections scheduled for October 6. \par \par \uc2  Many analysts, however, see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovering after a new government begins to indicate its positions on economic policy. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, according to a recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market survey, the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen ending 2002 at about BRL2.90 per dollar.\par     Newspaper website: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.folha.com.br"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.folha.com.br}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Brasilia Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 9965-6883,\par gerald.jeffrisdowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020929dy9t000cy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
