\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends At BRL3.126/Dlr Vs BRL3.105 Wednesday \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2002\par 21:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Brazil's real weakened Thursday, dragged lower by lingering concerns about the pace of recovery in the world's largest economy and how a slowdown there may delay a rebound in economic activity here. \par \par \uc2  The real shed 2.1 centavos to close at BRL3.126 to the dollar, following a downturn in U.S. equity markets following worse-than-expected jobless data. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , down 26% so far this year, closed Wednesday at BRL3.105. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling $50 million in 77-day dollar repurchase agreements and $43.9 million in six-month export credit lines. \par \par \uc2  Yet traders said President George W. Bush's call on the United Nations to support the U.S. in taking action against Iraq fueled fears of war on a day when Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan also warned of continued pressures on the U.S. federal budget outlook. \par \par \uc2  "Things look pretty ugly overseas and there's not much reason for optimism," said a Sao Paulo-based trader. \par \par \uc2  On the local front, a presidential poll was less favorable than expected. The Vox Populi survey showed the government's candidate Jose Serra stuck at 19% in second, countering expectations of a steady rise in the run-up to the Oct. 6 first-round vote. Front-runner Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva of the Workers' Party advanced three points to 39%. \par \par \uc2  There is still hope that Serra's strategy of late to attack Lula's lack of experience in television commercials may bear fruit in the coming weeks. However, a Middle East conflict could undo much of the improvement in sentiment, as Brazil is a net importer of oil and relies on foreign capital to finance much of its growth. \par \par \uc2  "Further improvements on the Serra front in the coming weeks should have positive impacts on Brazilian assets and the real, but a U.S. attack against Iraq, and its potential impacts on risk aversion and oil prices, will at least neutralize and possibly reverse those impacts," wrote Ricardo Amorim, head of Latin America research at IDEAglobal in New York. \par \par \uc2  By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3145-1481 adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020912dy9c0019g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
