\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends Weaker At BRL3.100 Vs BRL3.062 Monday \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2002\par 22:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Rattled by slumping markets and heightened risk aversion overseas, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended weaker Tuesday despite an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sale of export credits by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The real closed at BRL3.100 per dollar, compared with BRL3.062 at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sale of $50 million in export credits, which helped boost the supply of dollars on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, saw demand of about $120 million. \par \par \uc2  The size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't disclosed. \par \par \uc2  During the session, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Arminio Fraga said that a tough external environment is limiting chances for an interest rate cut to the current base rate of 18.00%. \par \par \uc2  The real has lost about 2.9% of its value since Friday, when it was trading at BRL3.01 and analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might cut rates if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held steady around the BRL3.00 level. \par \par \uc2  But Fraga noted that signs of renewed lending here by foreign banks are very encouraging. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's national development bank, or BNDES, received commitments for $300 million in trade financing from an Asian lender late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened despite a Vox Populi poll for the country's October presidential election showing government-backed candidate Jose Serra is technically tied for second place with arch rival Ciro Gomes, a former Ceara state governor. \par \par \uc2  Serra, who is viewed as market friendly, and Gomes are each hoping to make it past an Oct. 6 first round vote to face frontrunner Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in an Oct. 27 runoff. \par \par \uc2  The market also shrugged off a poll by survey firm Ibope that showed Serra has now overtaken Gomes in the state of Sao Paulo, Brazil's biggest electorate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479;\par terry.wade@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020903dy93001bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
