\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends At BRL2.910/Dlr Vs BRL3.020 Wednesday \b0\par\par\uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2002\par 21:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- A larger-than-expected $30 billion International Monetary Fund rescue package for Brazil boosted the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, though investors are still unsure about foreign banks' willingness to resume lending to local companies ahead of the October presidential election. \par \par \uc2  The real opened at BRL2.860 to the dollar and hit an intraday low of BRL2.930 before settling at BRL2.910 to the dollar, its strongest close since July 22. Wednesday, the real gained 9.5 centavos to BRL3.020. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the IMF package, the biggest of the Fund's history, restores confidence in a nation that saw its bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall so fast in recent weeks to the point that, for a few days, a default was appeared imminent. \par \par \uc2  But Thursday's rally was interrupted by a number of transactions that had been put on hold ever since the real hit the unimaginable level of BRL3.610 during nervous intraday trading last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The IMF package is large and important, but it's going to take a while before the local market returns to normal," said Alexandre Vasarhelyi, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk at ING Barings in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  "Some investors seeking to do (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) hedging, importers, people seeking to send funds to offshore accounts, they were all waiting for a respite to do business," he added. \par \par \uc2  Market players were quick to say that the IMF's decision to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use an additional $10 billion from the country's international reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market was by far the most important feature of the new IMF program. \par \par \uc2  The decision prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy and introduce an element of surprise to it. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Arminio Fraga said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would from now on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when deemed necessary, halting a program that called for daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $50 million that had been in place since early July. He also suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively going forward, saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the IMF's green light to do \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of up to $3 billion in a moving 30-day period. \par \par \uc2  The first actions under the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy took place as soon as Thursday. In addition to selling an undisclosed sum of dollars on the spot market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold $50 million worth of 85-day repos at a maximum exchange rate of BRL2.962554. \par \par \uc2  Yet, traders say the Brazilian economic outlook remains uncertain as two opposition candidates are leading in the polls for Brazil's presidency, raising concern that the country may shift toward unorthodox or market-unfriendly policies. \par \par \uc2  Also, one of the country's three main presidential candidates, Ciro Gomes of the center-left Labor Front, is yet to announce his formal support for the IMF agreement. Front-runner Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva of the left-wing Workers' Party did so earlier Thursday. Government-backed Jose Serra also said he's in favor of the agreement. \par \par \uc2  The main indication of confidence would be a return of foreign financing and credit lines to the country, say traders, which isn't happening just yet. \par \par \uc2  But there one important positive sign Thursday. The September \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures contract finished implying a rate that equaled the spot rate for the first time in nearly two months. Recently, the forward rate was trading below the spot rate, a market anomaly that only occurs when there's too much demand for physical dollars amid perceived conversion and counterparty risk. \par \par \uc2  -By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3145-1481; adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020808dy8800196\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
