\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends At BRL3.020/Dlr Vs BRL3.115 Tuesday \b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2002\par 21:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real rallied Wednesday, boosted by expectations that the International Monetary Fund will soon provide the nation with a fresh aid package that could extend into 2003. \par \par \uc2  The real added 9.5 centavos to end at BRL3.020 to the dollar, also supported by rumors that the upcoming presidential poll will show that the government-backed candidate still stands a chance of winning. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the real gained 10.5 centavos to close at BRL3.115. \par \par \uc2  Talk is that the new IMF agreement, which investors expect to be announced as soon as late Wednesday, would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  power. Also, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be allowed to use part of the IMF funds to help restore scarce commercial credit lines for Brazilian companies, according to market rumors. \par \par \uc2  "If the rumors are true, and I've no reason to believe they aren't, it becomes more difficult for people to bet against the real," said a Sao Paulo-based trader. \par \par \uc2  President Fernando Henrique Cardoso had lunch with Finance Minister Pedro Malan, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Arminio Fraga, Planning Minister Guilherme Dias and Presidential Chief of Staff Pedro Parente Wednesday, suggesting that an official announcement about the IMF deal may come soon. \par \par \uc2  But the Finance Ministry said it had no news on the IMF agreement just yet and wouldn't comment on any rumors. \par \par \uc2  Market players said the new agreement would include $2 billion in new IMF aid funds, plus $2.5 billion in World Bank loans. \par \par \uc2  In addition, talk is that the $7 billion of IMF funds that Brazil has already drawn down from an existing $15.5 billion facility may be used to back commercial credit lines for local firms. \par \par \uc2  The Fund also would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use an extra $5 billion from the country's international reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market. \par \par \uc2  On the October elections front, rumors started to circulate that an Ibope poll set for release Thursday evening would show opposition candidate Ciro Gomes - who is second in the polls - falling by as many as five percentage points. That would mark an interruption in Gomes's fast-rising trend, fueling hope that lagging government-backed candidate Jose Serra, now third, still stands a chance of making it to a runoff vote Oct. 27. \par \par \uc2  In the latest July 27-29 Ibope poll, Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva of the left-wing Workers' Party rose to 34% from 33%, while challenger Gomes dropped to 25% from 26%. Support for Serra rose to 14% from 13%. Voting intentions for former Rio de Janeiro governor Anthony Garotinho remained at 11%. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market as part of its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program. The institution said it would sell $50 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily and roll over all dollar repos coming due this month in a total August program of at least $1.84 billion. \par \par \uc2  -By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3145-1481; adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020807dy870015h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
