\par\par \b \uc2  THE BOTTOM LINE: Spanish Blue Chips Suffer In Brazil \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mark Beresford and Jonathan House \par \uc2 1,352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2002\par 11:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  MADRID -(Dow Jones)- The decline of the Brazilian real is posing an increasing threat to the earnings and balance sheets of Spain's largest companies. \par \par \uc2  Investor concern about Brazil's ability to service its debt, combined with fears that the presidency could fall into the hands of a left-leaning candidate in October, pushed the Brazilian real down 19% against the dollar in July alone. That may now force Spain's blue chips into additional provisions, write downs, and asset sales, and explains much of the recent slump in the IBEX-35 index, down 16% over the last month. \par \par \uc2  The crisis is weighing heavily on the earnings and capital ratios of Spain's two largest banks, Santander Central Hispano SA (STD) and Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria SA (BBV). It's also weakening the key earnings to debt ratios of telecom giant Telefonica SA (TEF), and prompting ratings agencies to downgrade the companies' bonds. \par \par \uc2  "But it's wider concerns than just the technical ones on debt," said Goldman Sachs credit analyst Felix Kaiser. "The real worry is that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  gets a more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  government and the environment for Telefonica and other companies in Brazil worsens. Brazil has performed really well for Telefonica, but that could change." \par \par \uc2  Telefonica's shares have dropped 40% so far this year, while SCH and BBVA shares are both down 36%. \par \par \uc2  Given the importance of Brazil to their businesses, withdrawal from the country isn't an option for any of the companies, even in the nightmare scenario of a leftist election victory, debt default, and the imposition of capital controls. \par \par \uc2  There are, too, strong cultural ties with Latin America and Spanish companies have stuck it out through the even graver crisis in Argentina. \par \par \uc2  Of the two banks, SCH has a much larger exposure to Brazil with total investment of around EUR7.39 billion and 8.3% of total assets in the troubled country, compared with investment of EUR1.5 billion and 1.9% of assets for BBVA. \par \par \uc2  Last week, SCH posted a fall in profits as weaker Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  resulted in lower revenues, and a EUR190 million loss of Brazilian government debt resulted in a 43% decline in trading profits. \par \par \uc2  The bank may have to establish provisions to cover further losses of its $6.5 billion portfolio of Brazilian government debt. \par \par \uc2  And charges against reserves of around EUR1.2 billion to account for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation lowered the bank's core capital ratio (minus preferred shares) to 4.56% from 5.15% at the end of the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  Core capital includes a bank's equity capital - which includes ordinary and preferred shares - and retained earnings minus goodwill. It measures the amount freely available for a bank to absorb losses without having to stop trading. Preferred shares are normally excluded from the calculation because, as they require guaranteed dividend payments, they are considered lower quality capital. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Spain recommends banks maintain a ratio of core capital minus preferred shares of 6%. \par \par \uc2  Even before it published its results, SCH was downgraded by Standard & Poor's Corp. Following the earnings, Moody's Investors Service Inc. placed the bank's ratings under review. \par \par \uc2  SCH is now under pressure to sell off some of the stakes it holds in Spanish companies and banks around the world, although the bank's management admits market conditions aren't encouraging and sales would reduce its cushion to cover further losses from Latin America. \par \par \uc2  The alternative, however, would be to hold a rights issue, diluting shareholder equity and reducing earnings per share. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect SCH to realize capital gains before resorting to a rights issue.The bank said its investment portfolio held latent capital gains of EUR5 billion at the end of the first half including its 20% stake in Spanish oil company Compania Espanola de Petroleos SA (E.CES) and a 12% stake in utility Union Fenosa SA (E.FEN). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Telefonica Cashflows Under Threat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Telefonica has invested around EUR24 billion in Brazil since 1998, and\par about a quarter of its total EBITDA and cashflow comes from there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday, Moody's put Telefonica's A2 debt rating on downgrade review\par "on concerns related to the uncertainties in Brazil, ahead of the\par October general elections."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market now anticipates negative action from Standard & Poor's.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While a Telefonica spokeswoman said 99.3% of its EUR1.5 billion debt\par in Brazil is hedged, financial gains made from hedging aren't included\par in the EBITDA line, so don't help offset the deterioration in the EBITDA\par to debt ratio.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Felix Kaiser at Goldman Sachs said the fall of the real could require\par Telefonica to write down the value of its Brazilian assets. After the\par drop in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the beginning of 1999, Telefonica made a EUR717\par million write down of its assets there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Key to the Moody's review will be Telefonica's decision to freeze its\par expansion in European 3G, which will save it billions of euro in capital\par expenditure and operating losses, potentially mitigating the effects of\par Brazil.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, some bears argue too much of the company's ability to pay\par down debt and distribute dividends is still hinged on the repatriation\par of cash from Latin America.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Lehman Brothers warned in a downgrade note last week: "The decision to\par pay a dividend is laudable, but we note that 60% of deleveraging post\par the dividend comes from Latin America."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The company's repatriation of cash will only add to the outflow of\par capital that is contributing to the regional crisis and to the fall of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the real, and could prompt action from the Brazilian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moody's said: "The review process will mainly focus on the potential\par impact on Telefonica's future free cash flow of the high volatility of\par the real as well as the hypothetical measures which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par might consider in the future to stabilise the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And observers warn that Telefonica's wireline business in Spain,\par currently the source of the bulk of its cashflow, is under increasing\par pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Standard & Poor's said in its latest comment July 25: "The primary\par ratings focus will continue to be the impact of the volatile financial\par and political environment in Brazil...and regulatory pressures in\par domestic fixed-line \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    BBVA Faces Indirect Risks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although BBVA posted an 8.9% fall in first half net profit and gave a\par full-year warning in line with SCH's, Brazil is seen having less of an\par impact on the bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BBVA said it had charged about EUR950 million against reserves for\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation, which helped to lower its core capital ratio\par (minus preferred shares) to 5.9%, which although lower than the 6%\par recommended by the Bank of Spain, remains considerably better than\par SCH's.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Brazil could affect BBVA through an investment portfolio that\par carries significant exposure there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BBVA said a EUR209 million provision made to account for a EUR4.8\par billion charge made by Telefonica, primarily to restructure European 3G\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is one of the main factors behind its expected decline in\par 2002 profits.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Continued meltdown in the Brazilian economy could also force BBVA to\par provision against losses there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We caution that BBVA's exposure to Brazil is by no means immaterial,"\par Bear Stearns warned in a research note.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Spain's second largest electricity company Iberdrola SA (E.IBR) has\par also suffered from its exposure to Brazil, which accounts for 3.6% of\par operating profit. Iberdrola charged EUR47 million against reserves in\par the first half on account of the decline in the real.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Regardless of the extent of their Brazilian exposure, the real risk\par for the Spanish companies is that a crisis which originally seemed\par contained to Argentina could now extend from Tierra del Fuego in the\par south all the way up to the Rio Grande.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Mark Beresford, Dow Jones Newswires; +34-91-3958123;\par mark.beresford@dowjones.com and Jonathan House, Dow Jones Newswires;\par 34-91-395-8121; jonathan.house@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  5008 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020807dy87000ic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
