\par\par \b \uc2  ODJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Mkt Hoped For More Aggressiveness \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2002\par 21:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones Commodities Service \par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Brazil Tuesday said it will continue\par with its $50 million daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program in August even though the plan\par failed to keep the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from hitting record low levels this month.\par Local markets shrugged off the announcement, which frustrated expectations\par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more aggressively as the Brazilian\par real is losing ground fast. The real didn't react and was quoted at BRL3.300\par to the dollar, a record intraday low, during late trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monetary Policy Director Luiz Fernando Figueiredo said the August\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will total $1.835 billion, split between spot market sales and\par dollar repurchase agreements. He said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will sell $1.1 billion\par in U.S. dollars on the spot market, while the remaining $735 million may\par involve spot sales and repos.\par Figueiredo added that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may increase \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  next\par month beyond the $1.835 billion mark if liquidity dries up.\par In July, the central banks said it would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to the tune of $1.5\par billion, also split between repos and spot sales.\par The real has lost as much as 30% of its value this year to date. Traders say\par there is a lack of dollars on the local market as international credit markets\par are shut for Brazilian corporate risk. There is fear that the dramatic\par weakening of the real may infect the country's economic fundamentals and\par compromise its ability to stay current on debt payments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1946GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djcs000020020730dy7u00qpa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
