\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real At BRL3.22 Vs BRL3.29, Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2002\par 21:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- After weakening to as far as BRL3.29 per dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 1920 GMT, the real was trading stronger at BRL3.185 from BRL3.220 just after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real has fallen as much as 8.5% this session.  The real closed at BRL3.105 per dollar Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently sells about $50 million a day as part of a daily strategy to provide liquidity to the market, though traders said they thought the size of Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was larger than usual. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Falling Brazilian external bond prices and rumors of an unfavorable presidential poll result triggered the selloff earlier Monday, said traders. \par \par \uc2  Contributing to the selling were comments made by U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill over the weekend. Local market players interpreted his comments as a sign that the Bush administration won't back a transitional support package for Brazil from the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  -Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020729dy7t0015f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppic