\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Ends At BRL2.897/Dlr; Worst Close Ever \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2002\par 21:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Brazil's real ended at its lowest close ever Wednesday, largely reacting to a surprise interest rates cut to 18.00% from 18.50%. \par \par \uc2  The real ended at BRL2.897 to the dollar, slightly weaker than its worst previous close of BRL2.896 July 1. Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at BRL2.872 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A Sao Paulo-based trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to cut rates was unexpected and investors were still trying to position themselves, increasing volatility in the real. \par \par \uc2  Also, traders said investors were still concerned about the political outlook ahead of presidential elections in October. \par \par \uc2  They added there was talk that government-backed candidate Jose Serra's campaign could lose running mate Rita Camata. The rumor was dismissed by Serra's Brazilian Social Democracy Party, or PSDB, and by a spokesperson for Camata. \par \par \uc2  If true, though, a Rita pullout would be bad news for Serra's already flagging campaign. Late Tuesday, he fell to third in the polls behind front-runner Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, of the Workers' Party, and leftist Ciro Gomes. \par \par \uc2  Camata is seen as key to helping dour Serra be more appealing to voters. Investors are rooting for Serra, who is considered to be market-friendly. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $100 million in 60-day repurchase agreements at a rate of BRL2.920 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Banks buying the contracts agreed to sell dollars back to the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Sept. 17. The sale of the contracts was held to roll over similar repos coming due. \par \par \uc2  The size of the offering is double the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that come in the form of dollar spot sales, or repos. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it sold $50 million onto the market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did little to help bolster the real during the session\par amid investor unease.\par    -By Paula Lace and Anthony Dovkants; Dow Jones Newswires;\par 55-11-3145-1478; brazil@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020717dy7h00141\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
