\par\par \b \uc2  Chilean peso firms on  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2002\par 21:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Chile, July 3 (Reuters) - Chile's peso ended firmer on Wednesday, following gains in the Brazilian real after the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the weakened \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  At closing, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 694.50/695.00 pesos per U.S. dollar, up 0.71 percent from Tuesday's close of 699.50/699.80 but still down about 5 percent since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso would remain volatile until turbulence in Brazilian markets subsided, probably after that country's presidential election in October. \par \par \uc2  "Even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injects liquidity to defend the real, there is still a lot of pressure in the market and that is affecting the peso," said Gabriela Clivio, analyst with Santiago brokerage. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's battered real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded on Wednesday after the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would inject $1.5 billion into the market in July to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real firmed to 2.845 per dollar from Tuesday's close of 2.895. \par \par \uc2  Traders in Chile's peso, battered last year by the Argentine financial crisis, have now turned to Brazil's financial markets as a barometer of investor confidence in the region. \par \par \uc2  Chilean traders said they expected the real to continue losing ground despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's financial markets have been whipped in recent weeks by fears economic problems could hinder its debt payments and by the lead in polls of a leftist presidential candidate. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020703dy730111k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
