\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging debt-Downgrade hurts  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 , CenBank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  helps. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hugh Bronstein \par \uc2 448 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2002\par 18:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 3 (Reuters) - Brazilian sovereign bonds led the emerging debt market slightly lower Wednesday as investors tried to balance Tuesday's credit rating downgrade against news the government will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  downgrade scared a few people and bonds traded down," one emerging debt trader said. "Then the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which gave the market a bit of a pop. These two things offset each other, but Brazil is going to end the day down." \par \par \uc2  Brazil slumped 2.7 percent in total returns at midday, while the market as a whole edged 0.8 percent lower, according to JP Morgan's Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus. For the year, Brazil, which has been battered by political uncertainty ahead of the October presidential election, is down 21.6 percent, while the wider index is down 0.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the market is severely underweight Brazil and there's risk aversion out there, so there are still some sellers," said Jim Barrineau, a vice president in emerging markets research at Alliance Capital Management. "Trading is active for the day before July 4th." \par \par \uc2  The market was set to close early ahead of the U.S. Independence Day holiday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with a combination of dollar sale \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the value of $1.5 billion in the month of July, to boost liquidity in the market after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to record lows. \par \par \uc2  The bank said it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with $100 million per day through the rest of this week, after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday with $300 million. Through the rest of the month from Monday next week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with $50 million per day. \par \par \uc2  Standard & Poor's on Tuesday lowered Brazil's sovereign rating, citing growing difficulties in managing its public debt. \par \par \uc2  Brazilian debt prices have plunged in recent weeks, pushing interest rates to levels not seen in more than three years and raising the cost of servicing its estimated $250 billion debt profile on worries about a victory by left-leaning Workers Party candidate Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. \par \par \uc2  S&P cut Brazil's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to B-plus - four notches below investment grade - from BB-minus and its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt rating to BB from BB-plus. \par \par \uc2  "Brazil is up and down," another debt trader said of Wednesday's market. "No one knows what the right level is for Brazil to trade at, considering the political side of the story and the economic side." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020703dy7300wew\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
