\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's Real Opens At BRL2.790 Vs BRL2.770 End Thurs \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2002\par 14:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian real continued to weaken against the dollar at the open Friday, as the market awaited signs of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1250 GMT, the real was trading at BRL2.790 per dollar  compared with BRL2.770 per dollar at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real's going to sink into the BRL2.80 per dollar range," said a trader in Sao Paulo. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market repeatedly this week to try to ease pressure on the real, but has so far seen limited success in calming investors' nerves. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after a battery of other measures  adopted last week, including the announcement of a $10 billion drawdown on a loan from the International Monetary Fund, a hike in bank reserve requirements to 15% from 10%, swaps of domestic debt to shorten maturities, and buybacks of overseas debt. \par \par \uc2  Nonetheless, the country's risk rating as measured by the JP Morgan EMBI+ this week rose to more than 1,500 points, second only to Argentina. \par \par \uc2  Market participants, meanwhile, are waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to formally draw down on its available IMF loan  funding to determine to what extent it is willing to inject  foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the local market. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's real has lost more than 17% against the dollar this year amid market nervousness over the presidential succession to take place after the country's October 6 elections. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide, recent market surveys released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  show the real is expected to end the year at around BRR2.50 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-61-9965-6883; gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020621dy6l000s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
