\par\par \b \uc2  Charting Trends: Getting Real About  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Stephen Cox, CMT \par \uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2002\par 22:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Last week's chart of USD/BRL might  have been a roadmap for this week's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This afternoon the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  performed two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, buying the  Brazilian real to the tune of $50 million. \par \par \uc2  USD/BRL is trading at 2.7110 late in the Tuesday New York session. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has done its job, USD/BRL will sink to 2.6444 or to 2.6316 before the month is out. \par \par \uc2  The point is that the fundamental influence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the charts last week just ahead of the past two \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, USD/BRL recorded a weekly high of 2.7945, the  high of a two-month uptrend. The high was recorded on June 12, just before \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, June 14. Last week's high practically represented a test of last October's high for the multi-year bull market, which was 2.8060 resistance. The market closed out last week in the middle of the week's high-low range. That was a technical signal of lost upside momentum and the possibility of a sell-off. \par \par \uc2  In other words, the time was right for a strengthening of the real against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  This isn't to say that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  necessarily had to happen. Certainly, it's not to say that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will work in the sense of meaningfully strengthening the real against the dollar, although last week's USD/BRL hit on long-term resistance puts the odds in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's favor. \par \par \uc2  In fact, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't have meaningfully strengthened the real unless USD/BRL falls below 2.6444 this  week. Late-day trading under 2.6444 on Friday implies an eventual move down to 2.6316 at least. And a move below 2.6316 would leave USD/BRL open to a serious technical breakdown. \par \par \uc2  A decisive move above 2.7210 means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2   has been foiled, according to the charts. In that case, USD/BRL will soon move up to 2.7930. \par \par \uc2  To read the latest Charting Markets technical newsletter  go to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnewswires.com/charting/ta.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnewswires.com/charting/ta.html}}}\par \par \uc2  For more technical analysis see: Dow Jones Newswires, N/DJTA; Telerate, page 4247; Bloomberg, NI DJTA; and Reuters  key word search "Charting Markets". \par \par \uc2  -By Stephen Cox; 201-938-2064; stephen.cox@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Stephen Cox, a chartered market technician, is chief technician for Dow Jones Newswires.) \par \par \uc2  Data by CSI, Commodity Research Bureau \par \par \uc2  70759 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020618dy6i00dqh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
