\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens -2:Traders Defy Ctrl Bk To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2002\par 15:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Investors continued to dump Brazilian reals at the open Wednesday, testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tolerance of a sinking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid growing worries that the government may fail to roll over a heavy load of dollar-linked debt maturing next next. \par \par \uc2  After ending Tuesday at its lowest close in seven and a half months at BRR2.712 to the dollar, the real opened at BRR2.732 and was extending losses. At around 1300 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was changing hands at BRR2.742. \par \par \uc2  Traders are growing concerned that Brazil may be en route to a debt crisis amid jitters ahead of the October presidential election and the collapse of its neighbor Argentina's economy, which is also making the life of another neighbor, Uruguay, extremely difficult these days. \par \par \uc2  "There's a complete mistrust in the country at the moment," said a Sao Paulo-based trader. "The market is now  defying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The real has lost about 8% of its value so far this month, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly introduced new accounting rules for mutual funds which ended up sparking debt worries. \par \par \uc2  Following the government's failed attempt Tuesday to sell fixed-rate treasury bills that mature before Brazil's Oct. 6 presidential election, the market is now growing worried that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid to use December 2002 derivatives to roll over maturing dollar-linked may fall through. \par \par \uc2  Market players are saying they'll demand high premiums to buy the lot of 12,500 December 2002 \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts at an auction later Wednesday - which may lead the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reject bids. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap offering, valued at $600 million, is designed to start the rollover process of an unusually-large  $2.4 billion maturity of dollar-linked debt due June 19. \par \par \uc2  "I don't what would be worse: the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rejecting bids or the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accepting to pay a high premium to place the swaps," said another Sao Paulo-based trader. \par \par \uc2  Such worries and the continued slide of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are prompting companies and rich individuals to seek greenback protection as well as send some of their money overseas. Cemig, a Minas Gerais state power utility, for instance, said Tuesday its board approved the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging for all its $600 million dollar-linked liabilities. \par \par \uc2  The government has said it can draw down from an existing $15 billion International Monetary Fund aid package  as well as sell dollars on the spot market. Brazil currently has about $8 billion in hard-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves it could use for spot-market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, market players shrugged off benign May inflation data unveiled earlier Wednesday. The government said the May consumer price index was 0.21%, below market expectations of 0.25% to 0.50%. During normal times, such a benign inflation figure would push markets higher as it would pave the way for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had signaled last month it would resume cutting rates at the June 18-19 policy meeting, but analysts said a rate reduction is becoming an increasingly remote possibility in view of the recent market's downturn. Nominal interest rates have been above 18% for nearly a year  and are among the world's highest in real terms. \par \par \uc2  By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3145-1481; adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020612dy6c000ti\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
