\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Real Ends Weaker At BRR2.712 As Mkt Tests Ctrl Bk \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2002\par 21:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Hit by worries over the government's ability to manage its hefty debt load, Brazil's real weakened sharply Tuesday as investors snapped up dollars in an attempt to avoid losses from a weakening local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With political uncertainties ahead of the October presidential elections contributing to the volatility, traders said the market is now testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended at BRR2.712 to a dollar, compared with BRR2.636 at Monday's close. Ten days ago, the real was at BRR2.510. \par \par \uc2  Among those looking for or planning to hedge are power company Cemig, which approved the use of hedging to protect up to 100% of the company's dollar-linked debt against \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations, a company official said Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a weakening real and hedging interest, traders say, will likely create a self-reinforing process that will force the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken further in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's net debt load as a percentage of gross domestic product has increased over the last several years and currently runs at about 54.5%, a ratio that weighs on the real. And with October elections approaching, investors reluctant to hold paper maturing after October have forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shorten the maturities it offers. \par \par \uc2  Left-wing presidential candidate Luis Inacio Lula da Silva is leading polls at about 40%, with government-backed candidate Jose Serra running around 20%. \par \par \uc2  As a result of investor concerns, the government has been busy swapping longer-term debt for short-term paper. Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  swapped more than BRR20 billion of bills. \par \par \uc2  A third of Brazil's BRR600 billion-plus public debt will mature in the short term and analysts say investor worries could complicate debt rollover and management \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Brazil has cash reserves of about BRR50 billion to ward-off debt jitters. \par \par \uc2  -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  With the sharp fall Tuesday, the real ended at its weakest level in about seven and a half months. On Oct. 30, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at BRR2.723 a dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020611dy6b00188\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
