\par\par \b \uc2  Eyeing  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Presidency, PT Vows More Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Adriana Arai \par \uc2 1,088 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2002\par 22:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian Workers' Party, with its candidate leading in the polls ahead of the October presidential election, is advocating more state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and increased public spending to reactivate growth in Latin America's largest nation. \par \par \uc2  While party leader and presidential contender Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva has toned down his anti-capitalism rhetoric and no longer talks about returning privatized companies to state control, Brazil's biggest left-wing group - better known by its Portuguese initials PT - says government subsidies are key to meet a wide range of goals, from boosting exports to fighting inflation. \par \par \uc2  It would be a break from nearly a decade of "excess liberalism and a certain dose of incompetence," says the PT's top economic adviser, Guido Mantega, who blames President Fernando Henrique Cardoso's free-market reform and stabilization policies for the low growth rates Brazil saw over the past seven and a half years. Since Cardoso took office in 1995, the annual growth rate has averaged 2.4%. \par \par \uc2  "When they floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they finally put economic policy on the right track. But the pace of improvement ever since hasn't been fast enough," Mantega told Dow Jones Newswires. "Three years later, the country has the same external vulnerability as before." \par \par \uc2  Since Cardoso abandoned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls in January 1999, fifteen days into his second term, exports have advanced 14% while imports declined 4%. A $6.6 billion trade deficit in 1998 turned into a surplus forecast at $4 billion this year, helping narrow Brazil's current account gap to $20 billion from $33 billion in the period. \par \par \uc2  But the PT's 53-year-old economist says \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  must use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost its trade surplus more rapidly. His plan involves across-the-board export subsidies and tax breaks or trade protection for certain industries, to encourage import substitution. \par \par \uc2  With less pressure to borrow, Mantega says Brazil would be able to pay less interest on its debt, have a less volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and resume growth. A trade surplus of $10 billion would be "comfortable," he adds, noting that tourism promotion efforts could slash the external deficit by another $1.5 billion in coming years. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Desire To Loosen Fiscal Policy Worries Market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The essence of the PT's recipe to pull Brazil out of the low growth,\par high interest trap is similar to a plan being proposed by Cardoso's\par hand-picked successor, Jose Serra, who also thinks the current account\par deficit is the country's main weaknesses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If effective, the proposed measures would translate into a big fiscal\par relief. Interest payments, currently running at above 7% of GDP\par annually, would no longer eat into the government's primary budget\par surplus of about 3.5% of GDP and, consequently, increase the public\par debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mantega says lower interest rates combined with an expected resumption\par of economic growth would significantly improve Brazil's net debt-to-GDP\par ratio, which currently stands at 54.5%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par So much so that Brazil would finally be ready to loosen fiscal policy\par after four consecutive years of belt-tightening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If you create conditions for interest rates to fall, you could reduce\par the primary budget surplus target, so long as the fiscal deficit is\par under control," said Mantega. "This administration failed to find\par instruments to reduce rates, so it shifted the focus to the primary\par surplus from the nominal fiscal deficit, which is what really matters,"\par he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par How much lower could the primary surplus be? "It depends on the pace\par of decline of interest rates, which is impossible to predict, as\par interest rates are set by market dynamics and cannot be cut by decree,"\par answers Mantega.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That's where the PT's policy intentions cause a few raised eyebrows in\par the financial community.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Though few economists would disagree with Mantega's remarks that\par Cardoso's tight-budget efforts have been largely undone by the high\par level of interest rates, they say maintaining a primary surplus at 3.5%\par of GDP in the next few years is imperative to keep Brazil's fiscal house\par in order.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cardoso, for example, did try to loosen fiscal targets when the\par economy was booming in 2000. But the attempt failed. In August 2000, he\par reduced the primary surplus goal to 3% for 2001 and 2.7% for 2002, from\par 3.35% and 3%, respectively. One year later, financial turmoil in the\par region and at home forced the Brazilian president to reset the targets\par at 3.35% in 2001 and 3.5% in 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, Mantega thinks Brazil can get away with running a fiscal\par deficit after interest payments of 4% to 4.5% of GDP, about where it\par stands now, as long as the debt-to-GDP ratio is at a "reasonable level."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 40% in opinion polls, PT's Lula says lowering rates and increasing\par public spending would all be a gradual process, emphasizing that\par "keeping fiscal responsibility and inflation under control are "a\par commitment of honor the Workers' Party has with 170 million Brazilians."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But market analysts say the PT's emphasis on social projects and the\par blatant desire to increase spending raise questions about whether Lula,\par if in command, would have the guts to cut the budget in times of crisis.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aware of the market's concerns about Brazil's fragile fiscal\par situation, Serra, for his part, has said he would maintain the 3.5%\par primary surplus target unchanged if elected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In local and state governments, the PT has shown it can be even more\par responsible when it comes to fiscal accounts than administrators from\par parties allied with Cardoso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Yet monetary policy is at stake this time around.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If elected, Lula said he would appoint a new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor who\par certainly won't be Arminio Fraga. Mantega, meanwhile, says the\par inflation-targeting regime Fraga introduced in 1999 would stay, but\par changes would be made and targets would be loosened. He says 5% sounds\par like a more reasonable number for annual inflation here than Fraga's\par 3.5% goal for 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The fight against inflation is much more complex than simply keeping\par interest rates higher," says Mantega.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This government is simply combating the symptoms, not the roots of\par inflation," he adds, noting the creation of a mass products market and\par less \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility in the face of a smaller current account\par deficit would also help keep inflation in check.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3145-1481;\par adriana.arai@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020530dy5u0018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
