\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  To Handle  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Exchange  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Online \b0\par\par\uc2 128 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2002\par 12:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will transfer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange market to an online system, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monetary Policy Directory Luiz Fernando Figueiredo said late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The changeover to the electronic system, known as Sisbex, will take place within 60 days. \par \par \uc2  Figueiredo said the new system would make \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  more transparent for the market. \par \par \uc2  Currently, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are handled with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 25 primary dealers over the phone. \par \par \uc2  The Sisbex system, which is administered in Rio de Janeiro, already handles approximately $250 million a day in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, or about 25% of the country's total volume. \par \par \uc2  -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 9965-6883, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020131dy1v000re\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
