\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Ends A Tad Stronger On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2001\par 22:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came to the real's rescue Wednesday and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  close slightly stronger, despite persistent concerns about the global economy. \par \par \uc2  The real closed one centavo stronger at BRR2.771 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  called an emergency auction of BRR1 billion in short-term dollar-linked T-bills as the real hit an intraday weak point of BRR2.791. Tuesday's close was BRR2.781, the second-worst ever. \par \par \uc2  "We saw a couple of (corporate) names shopping around for price quotes for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging, and when that happens, the real weakens, even if the company doesn't close the deal in the end," said a Sao Paulo-based \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  There has been large corporate demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging in recent months, in particular after the Sept. 11 acts of terrorism, as market participants believe the real could weaken further amid so much uncertainty about the global economic outlook. Some investment banks forecast the real as weak as BRR3.00 to the dollar by year end. \par \par \uc2  Such worries became evident at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction of dollar-linked T-bills, which also serve as protection against further \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the BRR1 billion lot of June 2002 dollar-indexed T-bills was more than twice oversubscribed, with demand reaching BRR2.18 billion. The paper sold for an average annualized rate of 8.04%. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, benign September inflation data helped bring money market rates slightly lower as it reinforced the view that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't likely have to raise interest rates to control prices. \par \par \uc2  Futures contracts finished projecting the interbank rates at 22% in early January, down from 22.35% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The September consumer price index was 0.28%, the lowest rate in 11 months, and in line with market expectations. \par \par \uc2  The 30% depreciation of the real this year is inflating public debt, fueling inflation and forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep monetary policy tight. But it's also helping Latin America's biggest nation narrow its external financing needs by means of trade. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the country's international reserves inched lower to $39.602 billion Tuesday from $39.662 billion Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Web Site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcb.gov.br/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bcb.gov.br}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3145-1481 adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011010dxaa00k5u\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjus